# `~Module.fn` must name a function of that module, or a `make` function of
# the type it names (`~String.upperCase`). `upcase` is neither: the capture
# passed the check and failed when it ran ("`String.upcase` is not a
# function" on the walker, `badarg` on BEAM).
main do
  IO.printLine("${["ab"].map(~String.upcase)}")
end
